description:
pkix-lint/src/lib.rs LintRunner::run_chain (lines 798-804):

    let mut all = Vec::new();
    for (i, cert) in chain.iter().enumerate() {
        ...
        all.extend(self.run_cert(cert, kind, i, now_unix));
    }

Vec::new() allocates no capacity. For a chain of N certs with M lints each, there are N reallocations during extend (amortized, but still). The total finding count is predictable: chain.len() * self.lints.len(). Pre-allocating avoids all reallocations:

    let mut all = Vec::with_capacity(chain.len() * self.lints.len());

This is in the hot path for any caller running a full chain evaluation.

Category: R5 (HashMap::new/Vec::new without capacity hint in hot paths)
